 PASSED` (dev+release × default+`--no-default-features`) |\n\nSurface: the whole library is `void driver(float x)` (+ `static print_hex`). Symbol parity is exact (`driver` only). The error surface is provably **empty** — zero `return`s, asserts, range or null checks in the C — so Phase C rows were derived as hostile/degenerate float inputs (sNaN payloads, ±0, subnormals, `0x80..0xff` byte zero-extension, FLT_MIN/MAX boundaries) each asserted against an exact expected stdout.\n\n## Two real harness bugs found and fixed\n\n1. **`cargo test` never rebuilds a `cdylib`** — the suite was silently comparing against a stale `.so`. Proven by a mutation (`%02X`) that went undetected. `tests/common/mod.rs` now builds the cdylib itself into a separate `--target-dir` (separate build lock, no deadlock) and asserts both `.so`s are newer than their sources.\n2. **libtest's own buffered progress output leaked into the fd-1 capture**, causing 8 bogus Phase B failures. Fixed by flushing both stdio layers before stealing fd 1 and pinning `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1` via `.cargo/config.toml`.\n\nAfter fix 1, six independent mutations of the Rust source (`%02X`, `%x`, `len`=3, dropped newline, reversed byte order, `signed char`) were each caught by 16–20 tests — the suite has teeth.\n\nTwo of my own table entries were wrong and were corrected against the C (which is ground truth): expected output for `0x7fffffff` is `ffffff7f`, not `ffff7f7f`. `c_src/` was not modified (only `c_src/build/`, as instructed).","ttft_ms":2803,"type":"result","duration_ms":575123,"uuid":"998a8b98-b851-40e4-89a1-f7f05db0b309","ttft_stream_ms":2656,"time_to_request_ms":53,"first_content_frame_ms":2656,"queued_turn_count":0}
